{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The eagle</b> — I do not know how it flies in the firmament, in the air of the heavens, yet it does not know where it will alight upon the earth." "Another interpretation: the way of the eagle — that it leaves no path behind it by which a person might see where it passed. And so all of them." "<b>And the way of a snake</b> — how is it possible to go upon a rock without legs, and it does not know in what place it can rest." "<b>And the way of a ship</b> — it is in danger to cross the heart of the sea, and it does not know to which destination the wind will carry it." "<b>With a young woman</b> — in his lying with her, that he does not fear HaShem in transgressing the commandment 'You shall not commit adultery,' and he does not consider its end."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:36.830562289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}